From 98b986243cdc8fbe53269fdf9e9a4ada653cdf24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 07:53:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] imx585: report each mode's sensor window as its crop
 rectangle

Every supported_modes[] entry carried .crop = {0, 0, output width, output
height}, so libcamera's analogCrop (and Core's ScalerCropMaximum) said
(0,0)/<mode size> for all 21 modes and nothing could tell a binned or
windowed mode from a full-field one. The crop is now the window in native
sensor pixels: full width, the WINMODE start row minus the 12-row active
offset, and the height before binning. The 4K and 16-bit entries are
unchanged. Register programming does not read .crop (set_pad_format copies
it into the subdev state only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T93jucKMhWYnQM1yyFVkbH
---
